the wave theory of light

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:04.409
was very useful for a time but it could
not explain

00:01:04.409 --> 00:01:08.229
the photoelectric effect. this was the
observation

00:01:08.229 --> 00:01:12.430
that if a certain metal plate is
irradiated with light an electron is

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:13.150
ejected

00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:16.960
which can be detected when it interacts
with a positively charged wire or

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:17.799
plate sensor.

00:01:17.799 --> 00:01:22.619
the incongruity was that the ability of
the light to eject an electron

00:01:22.619 --> 00:01:26.770
depends only on its frequency and not
its intensity

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:31.710
so if the beam was below a certain
frequency even a very intense beam

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:35.439
with a lot of light could not eject an
electron whereas

00:01:35.439 --> 00:01:38.890
above a certain frequency the faintest
beam possible

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:42.570
could do it. this seem strange and a
famous fellow named

00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:47.030
albert Einstein solved the problem by
extending a concept developed by max

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:47.590
planck

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:51.920
just five years prior. planck proposed that
energy is not continuous

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:55.740
but rather is quantized, that is all
energies

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:58.860
are multiples of the smallest fundamental
unit of energy

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:03.170
the plank energy. in fact quantum theory
went on to show that everything is

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:03.909
quantized

00:02:03.909 --> 00:02:07.439
space and time too, so you can't
infinitely subdivide them

00:02:07.439 --> 00:02:11.110
you'll eventually get to a smallest
thing that can't be divided further

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:12.900
but more on that in the physics course.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:16.750
einstein extended what planck said
about energy

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:20.510
and rationalized that light must also be
made of quanta

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:24.590
which he called photons. these are
particles of light

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:29.220
this explains the photoelectric effect
because an electron is ejected

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:33.510
when struck by a singular photon with
sufficient energy

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:37.220
it only takes one photon so even the
faintest beam

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:41.659
above a certain frequency will be able
to do it but if none of them are of that

00:02:41.659 --> 00:02:42.720
minimum energy

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:47.470
no matter how many photons strike the
sample an electron will not be ejected

